{{also|Purple}}
==English==
{{wp}}
[[File:Color icon purple v2.svg|thumb|Various shades of '''purple'''.]]
{{Wiktionary:Picture dictionary/en:color}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:purpel|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|purple}}, {{m|enm|purpel}}, from {{inh|en|ang|purpul|t=purple|pos=adjective}}, taken from {{der|en|ang|purpure|t=purple colour|pos=noun}}, from {{der|en|la|purpura|t=purple dye, shellfish}}, from {{der|en|grc|πορφύρα|t=[[purple-fish]]}}, perhaps of {{der|en|sem|-}} origin. {{dbt|en|purpura|purpure}}.
The sense of "imperial power" is from the wearing of the color purple by emperors and kings.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɜː.pl̩/|a=RP,AU}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɝ.pl̩/|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-purple.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpøːpl̩/|a=NZ,Wales}}
* {{IPA|en|/pʌɾpl̩/|a=Scotland}}
* {{IPA|en|/peːpl̩/|a=Scouse,square-nurse}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɛːpl̩/|a=Humberside,Teesside,square-nurse}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)pəl|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q3257809}}A colour between [[red]] and [[blue]]; [[violet]], though often closer to magenta.
#: {{color panel|web color|BF00FF}}
#: {{syn|en|blue-red}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost| book=IV| lines=596–597| text=Arraying with reflected '''Purple''' and Gold / The Clouds that on his Weſtern Throne attend.| year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|colour theory}} Any non-[[spectral]] colour on the [[line of purples]] on a colour [[chromaticity]] diagram or a [[colour wheel]] between violet and red.
# Cloth, or a [[garment]], dyed a purple colour; especially, a purple [[robe]], worn as an [[emblem]] of rank or [[authority]]; specifically, the purple robe or mantle worn by Ancient Roman emperors as the emblem of imperial dignity.
#: {{ux|en|to put on the imperial '''purple'''}}
#* {{RQ:Douay Bible|OT2|Song of Songs|7|5|341|Thy head as Carmelus: and the heares of thy head as a kings '''purple''' tyed to cundite pipes.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Imperial power.
#* '''1776-1788''', {{w|Edward Gibbon}}, ''{{w|The History of the Decline and Fall of the Roman Empire}}''
#*: He was born in the '''purple'''.
#* {{quote-journal|en|title={{smallcaps|Napoleon a Sainte Helene. Opinion d’un Medecin sur la Maladie de l’Empereur Napoleon, et sur la Cause de sa Mort; offerte a son Fils, au Jour de sa Majorite.}} Par ''S. Hereau'',{{nb...|Ancien Chirurgien de Madame Mere, et Premier Chirurgien de l’Emperatrice Marie Louise. 8vo. pp. 228. Paris. 1829.}}| editor=w:[[James Johnson (surgeon)|James Johnson]]|journal=The Medico-Chirurgical Review, and Journal of Practical Medicine| volume=X| issue=XX| location=London| publisher={{...|Published by}} S. Highley,{{nb...|174, Fleet Street, and Webb Street, St. Thomas’s Hospital, And all other Booksellers}}| month=March| year=1829| page=434| passage=When we picture to ourselves his &#91;{{w|Napoleon}}’s] dawning military genius at Toulon—his daring and decided politics in the storms of the Revolution—his Cæsarian ambition in assuming the '''purple'''—{{...|nospace=1}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1946|author=w:Bertrand Russell| title=History of Western Philosophy| section=I.29| passage=The immediate successors of Augustus indulged in appalling cruelties towards senators and towards possible competitors for the '''purple'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|mollusk species}}Any of various species of [[mollusk]]s from which [[Tyrian purple]] dye was obtained, especially the common [[dog whelk]].
# The [[purple haze]] [[cultivar]] of [[cannabis]] in the [[kush]] family, either pure or mixed with others, or by extension any variety of smoked [[marijuana]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Tipi Paul|title=Wanna Smoke?: The Adventures of a Storyteller| pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=4QyBN9A60qkC&pg=PA14&dq=smoke+some+purple&hl=en&ei=ziDTTrWHLMWRiQLNk7mwAw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=15&ved=0CHgQ6AEwDg|page=14| passage="Sure, some '''purple''' Owlsley."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Mark Arax|title=West of the West|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=vq1iKDq0YdUC&pg=PA221&dq=smoke+some+purple&hl=en&ei=ziDTTrWHLMWRiQLNk7mwAw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=20&ved=0CJABEOgBMBM| page=221| passage=“'''Purple''' smoke is no joke. Especially when it is real '''purple'''. The smell, taste, and high is easily one of the best in the world. One bowl of some '''purple''' Kush, and I'm done for a couple of hours.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Danielle Santiago|title=Allure of the Game|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=kRCN2TXAiQwC&pg=PA148&dq=smoke+some+purple&hl=en&ei=ziDTTrWHLMWRiQLNk7mwAw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=7&ved=0CE4Q6AEwBg|page=148| passage=She preferred to smoke some good '''purple''', but getting high wasn't an option.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} [[purpura|Purpura]].
# [[earcockle|Earcockle]], a disease of wheat.
# Any of the species of large butterflies, usually marked with purple or blue, of the genus {{taxlink|Basilarchia|genus}} (formerly {{taxfmt|Limenitis|genus}}).
#: {{ux|en|the banded '''purple'''}}
# A [[cardinalate]].
# {{lb|en|slang|US}} {{ellipsis of|en|purple drank}}.
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Magic|artist=Future|feat=T.I.|year=2012|album=Pluto|passage=Fishtailing out the parking lot leaving Magic / Sipping on the '''purple''' and the yellow, drinking magic}}
# {{lb|en|UK|slang}} {{synonym of|en|snakebite and black}}.
# A purple dye or pigment.
# A pen, pencil, crayon, etc., made of purple pigment.
# Something, or a part of a thing, which is purple.

